<title>HONG KONG: HK Bank of Canada Q2 net up 15.9 pct.</title>
<headline>HK Bank of Canada Q2 net up 15.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hongkong Bank of Canada, an indirectly wholly-owned unit of HSBC Holdings Plc, posted net profit of C$34.3 million for the three months to April 30, up 15.9 percent from C$29.6 million the previous year.  </p>
<p>Three months ended April 30 (in millions of Canadian dollars unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>    Net income per common share (CAD dollar)  0.12   vs  0.11</p>
<p>    Net interest income			     123.5  vs  117.6</p>
<p>    Other income					57.0   vs  38.2</p>
<p>    Net interest and other income		 180.5  vs  155.8</p>
<p>(including provision for credit losses)</p>
<p>    Net income					  34.3   vs  29.6</p>
<p>    Total assets					23,133 vs  20,478</p>
<p>    Total capital ratio (percent)		 9.3    vs  9.4</p>
<p>    Tier 1 capital ratio (percent)		5.2    vs  5.2</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6371</p>
</text>
